cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Computational supplement to "More Determinate and Less
  Settled": an agent-based test of Mitchell Berman's
  principled positivism
message: If you use this software or data, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kamper
    given-names: David G.
    affiliation: University of California, Los Angeles; University of Chicago Law School
    email: davidgkamper@ucla.edu
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a law review article giving Mitchell Berman's
  principled positivism its first systematic computational test. Contains
  ten notebooks, the shared simulation engine and sensitivity toolkit, the
  saved outputs behind every reported number, and the published figures.
  All results are computed on synthetic cases. The manuscript is under
  review and is not included in this deposit.
keywords:
  - legal philosophy
  - jurisprudence
  - legal positivism
  - agent-based modeling
  - computational legal theory
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
